# Frontend environment (Vite). Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored). Everything is optional.

# --- Map (Google Maps JavaScript API) ----------------------------------------------------
# The browser key. With it (and a Map ID) trips use the real Google map, loaded only when the map is
# first shown and never offline. Without it, trips draw the plain "Map preview" (stops, route and
# labels on a paper ground), which is also what runs in dev by default. The key ships in the bundle:
# restrict it by HTTP referrer (production domains and the localhost dev ports) and to the Maps
# JavaScript API, Places API (New) and Geocoding API. Put the real value in .env.development.local.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# The cloud-styled Map ID (a quiet light style with muted POIs). Advanced markers need one.
# In dev, DEMO_MAP_ID is used when this is empty; a production build needs a real ID.
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAP_ID=

# --- Local development with the mock trips server ----------------------------------------
# VITE_MOCK_TRIPS=1   (dev builds only: serves the trips API from an in-browser mock)
